A YAML 1.1 boolean word like `yes` is kept as a string and written single-quoted so it reloads as that string, not a boolean.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Test Plan
---
# Plan body

-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md answer=yes
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 ---
 title: Test Plan
+answer: 'yes'
 ---
 # Plan body
 
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: answer=yes
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Test Plan
answer: 'yes'
---
# Plan body

